1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,500
Why doesn't Hanzi Island use flashcards? Let's take a look.

2
00:00:05,454 --> 00:00:08,934
Pick your child's age and start the first character.

3
00:00:11,445 --> 00:00:16,653
First your child hears a whole sentence — the character appears in real context.

4
00:00:18,858 --> 00:00:23,224
One character is glowing. Your child finds it and taps it.

5
00:00:23,274 --> 00:00:28,290
Then guess which character it was. Wrong guesses are fine — no points lost.

6
00:00:29,435 --> 00:00:33,749
Next, see the pinyin and a word, and read along with the bunny.

7
00:00:33,799 --> 00:00:41,143
Kids who speak Chinese understand the sentence. Meaning first, then the shape — it sticks better and feels more fun.

8
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:45,604
Finally, listen and pick to check your child really knows it.

9
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:52,798
The address is on screen. Flashcards or sentences — what works for your child? Tell me in the comments.

